    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d633">

                <pb facs="0914" n="904" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg904"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.93/6–1545: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Truman to
                            Marshal Stalin
                    </hi><anchor n="61" xml:id="d633-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-06-15T15:03:00-04:00">15 June 1945—3:03 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>292. T. V. Soong departed by airplane today for Moscow via Chungking. He will
                    arrive Moscow before July 1st to discuss details of arrangements for
                    Soviet-Chinese agreements.</p>
                <p>Ambassador Hurley has been directed<anchor n="62" xml:id="d633-f2"/> to inform
                    Chiang Kai-shek on June 15th of Soviet conditions and to make every effort to
                    obtain the Generalissimo’s agreement therewith. Hurley is directed to inform
                    Chiang Kai-shek that the Yalta agreement will have the support of the United
                    States Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Truman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
